message: "If you use Ostrin in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Ostrin"
abstract: "Ostrin is an experimental general-purpose programming language focused on readability, physically meaningful types (quantities with dimensions) and safe-by-default concurrency. This repository contains a design-validation compiler and interpreter written in Rust."
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: MIT
